     "conductor",
     "rust",
     "non-metal"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Metals are shiny, hard, good conductors and can be beaten into sheets or drawn into wires. Gold, copper and iron are metals.\nIron reacts with air and water to form rust. We stop rust by painting, oiling or galvanising.\nNon-metals like carbon and sulphur are dull and break easily. Copper is used in wires because it conducts well."
    }
